From b87714496f92e8af4cbad3613f742a7c4ae47b76 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 23:21:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] U08: home performance, the static hero counts as the
 largest paint again

Diagnosis (the failing quality job on main, run 40382670533, and three
others): only Lighthouse performance fails, at 73, 74, 83 and 88 against
90; accessibility, best practices and SEO pass. Reproduced locally with
CI's flags (Lighthouse 13.5.0, mobile, simulated throttling): 87 to 90,
LCP 3.3 to 3.7 s. Two causes:

1. A race between the static hero and React. prerender-heads.mjs paints
   the hero into "/" so the largest paint is the first paint, but the
   bundle arrives before that frame's paint is recorded and React
   replaces the paragraph; Chrome drops the static paint as an LCP
   candidate and counts React's identical copy, so Lantern charges the
   whole bundle and its 4x-throttled evaluation to LCP. Delaying the
   bundle by 60 ms or more, or blocking it, makes the static paragraph
   the LCP at first paint.
2. The portrait, served from the legacy CloudFront host. A high-priority
   image that finishes before the observed LCP is charged to LCP: with a
   local stand-in for the CDN, a 2 MB portrait gave LCP 12.6 s and 73
   (the CI pattern); 184 KB gave 87 to 88.

Fixes:
- lib/static-hero.ts: on "/" only, main.tsx mounts React once the static
  hero's LCP entry is recorded (usually already buffered; at most 300 ms).
  Other paths (vercel.json serves the home HTML as the fallback), browsers
  without LCP, and hidden tabs mount at once. Tested in static-hero.test.ts.
- The portrait is fetchpriority="low" in Home.tsx and the prerendered
  hero: a thumbnail beside the name never competes with CSS, fonts and
  text, and stays out of LCP whatever its size.
- registerSW.js is deferred (vite-plugin-pwa injectRegister
  "script-defer"); it only waits for "load", so it no longer blocks the
  parser on every page.

Result, three runs each: 96 to 97 with the portrait unreachable; 92 to 95
with a 2 MB stand-in; 95 with 184 KB. LCP 2.4 to 2.8 s, FCP 1.8 to 2.0 s.

Moving the portrait in-house was blocked: this sandbox cannot reach
CloudFront. scripts/bring-portrait-home.mjs makes it one command where
the source is reachable (a URL, or the file James supplies): a 640 x 800
crop in client/public/images/ and PORTRAIT_URL repointed. AuthorBio now
reads PORTRAIT_URL, so the photograph is one constant. The other
CloudFront references are retired pages, admin data and seed scripts.

main.tsx drops an unused import (getLoginUrl) so the file lints clean.

